# Story Plain Prose

Chapter text in `Story/Chapters/` is narrative only. The story is the author's.

- Never paste reference shorthand, note labels, slang, or wiki jargon into the story.
- Keep coin math and craft facts in words Roland would think. Leave sheet terms in References / Notes.
- If a fact must land in prose, say it in ordinary language. Do not import the sheet name for it.
- Never say he knows seating, knows seating cold, has a sense for seating, or any Notes seating / seat-time / quality-only ability talk. Say he can draw reliably, make them reliably, or reliably make. Leave seating wording in Notes and References only.
- **Hard ban:** Never explain, justify, teach, or clarify anything unless the user explicitly orders that beat. No "so that," recipe recaps, or why-he-does-not-buy-X talk. Do the beat. Do not teach.
- Do not add "why this matters," background for the reader, or hand-holding. Assume the author and reader already know.
